@startuml TestingLayer3InfraIntegration
' SPEC source: internal/egress/integration_test.go
' Layer 3 — live egress topology with real containers, NO model.
' Build tag: //go:build integration — not compiled by default go test ./...
!includeurl https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/refs/heads/main/proveo.iuml
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam packageStyle rectangle

' purpose: the live egress topology Layer 3 stands up, and the three suites that
'          drive it — chain/CA, policy enforcement, broker-env mount
' covers: internal/egress/integration_test.go
' covers: internal/egress/**
'
' ── THREE SUITES OVER ONE TOPOLOGY, ALL GATED THE SAME WAY ──────────────────
' Each of the three checks PROVEO_EGRESS_INTEGRATION=1 and `docker` on PATH and
' skips otherwise, on top of the `//go:build integration` tag. Each stages its own
' squid config, builds a plan with BuildPlan, applies it with ExecRunner, registers
' plan.Teardown through t.Cleanup, and waits on plan.CAWaitPath (25s) before making
' a single request. Waits are conditions, never sleep-only: waitCond polls at 200ms
' and waitHTTPThroughProxy retries until curl reports exactly 200, reporting the
' last code and error when it gives up. The squid log dir is chmod 0777 so the
' squid image's own user can write to it whatever uid it runs as.
'
' 1. CHAIN + CA (TestFirewallIntegration). No provider pinned, so reads are allowed
'    by default. A real HTTPS GET to example.com must succeed through
'    agent → proxy → squid → internet with the generated CA trusted; the decrypted
'    request must appear in flows.ndjson; and a `--noproxy '*'` request must FAIL,
'    because the --internal agent network has no direct egress.
'
' 2. POLICY, END TO END THROUGH THE REAL MITM (TestFirewallPolicyIntegration). A
'    pinned provider (anthropic) gives the policy both a provider host and a secret
'    to protect — a fake `sk-ant-FAKE-SECRET-0123456789` written into broker.env.
'    A read is allowed; three shapes must each be blocked BEFORE leaving:
'      * a write (POST) to a non-allowlisted host,
'      * a GET to an exfil sink (webhook.site),
'      * a request carrying the known secret in the query string.
'    "Blocked" is read from curl's exit status — a policy block aborts the request,
'    so `curl -fsS` fails. Two further assertions make the block auditable rather
'    than merely effective: flows.ndjson must record `"decision":"blocked"`, and it
'    must NOT contain the secret value anywhere.
'
' 3. BROKER-ENV MOUNT (TestFirewallBrokerEnvMountIntegration). Proves the wiring a
'    host-side broker.env depends on, by inspecting the plan BEFORE applying it:
'    the proxy sidecar must carry PROVEO_EGRESS_PROVIDERS=cursor and
'    PROVEO_EGRESS_BROKER_ENVFILE=/broker/broker.env, and must bind-mount the inject
'    dir at /broker:ro. The topology must then still serve HTTPS, so a correct
'    mount cannot be traded for a broken chain.

title Layer 3 · Infra integration — real containers, no model\n(-tags=integration + PROVEO_EGRESS_INTEGRATION=1)

actor "integration test\n(BuildPlan + ExecRunner)\n//go:build integration" as Test <<actor>>

package "per-session egress topology (Docker)" as Topo {
 component "curl agent probe\ncurlimages/curl (no agent, no keys)" as Probe <<container>>
 component "agent-net\n--internal" as ANet <<queue>>
 component "proveo-egress\nTLS intercept + record" as Proxy <<container>>
 component "enforce-net\n--internal" as ENet <<queue>>
 component "squid:3128\nenforcement + write-pin" as Squid <<container>>
 component "egress-net\ninternet-capable" as XNet <<queue>>
 component "flows.ndjson\n(decrypted, no query string)" as Flows <<storage>>
 component "broker.env\n(host .env → inject)" as BrokerFile <<storage>>
}

cloud "internet (example.com)" as Net <<external>>

Test --> Topo : stage squid config + Apply plan
Test --> BrokerFile : writeBrokerEnv from host .env\n(CURSOR_API_KEY regression)
Probe --> ANet : HTTP_PROXY + trusts CA
ANet --> Proxy
Proxy --> Flows : record
Proxy --> ENet
ENet --> Squid
Squid --> XNet
XNet --> Net : allowed reads
BrokerFile ..> Proxy : mount /broker:ro

note bottom of Topo
Asserts the load-bearing invariants: HTTPS GET succeeds through
agent->proxy->squid->internet with the generated **CA trusted**; the decrypted
request is recorded to **flows.ndjson**; a proxy-bypassing request **fails**
(the --internal agent net has no direct egress). Broker-aware case: host .env
key → broker.env mounted; agent plan carries sentinel. Teardown via **t.Cleanup**.
Wait for CA file / HTTP ready — never fixed sleep-only sync.
Deterministic, keyless — no model is involved.
end note

note right of Test
Practices from Testcontainers (without the library): wait strategies,
t.Cleanup, env gate + docker LookPath skip. Orchestration stays BuildPlan
(no testcontainers-go — would duplicate owned topology).
Credential inject/strip proven in-process (egressproxy); this layer proves
network topology + broker mount wiring.
end note

note bottom of Flows
  **A block must be auditable, not just effective.**
  The suite asserts ""'decision':'blocked'"" is
  recorded AND that the fake secret never shows in
  the log — a proxy that blocks by logging the value
  it protected has moved the leak, not closed it.
end note

note bottom of Squid
  **Three block shapes, one allowed read.** A POST
  to a non-allowlisted host, a GET to an exfil sink,
  and the secret in a query string each fail before
  leaving — ""curl -fsS"" exiting non-zero IS the
  evidence, since a block aborts the request.
end note
@enduml
